1
00:00:00,625 --> 00:00:02,041
Summary

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,125
Throughout your radiation treatment,
it is very important to eat well

3
00:00:09,125 --> 00:00:12,041
and maintain the right level of calories.

4
00:00:12,041 --> 00:00:15,500
Ideally,
this means eating without restrictions

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,750
as much of the foods you wish to eat

6
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:20,291
to sustain a healthy body weight.

7
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:25,250
In this video, we explained common
nutrition challenges during treatment,

8
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,333
introduced you to your nutrition
support team

9
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:32,083
and explained how we can support you
if you lose weight.

10
00:00:32,375 --> 00:00:35,291
Again, the placement of a feeding tube,

11
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:40,166
either dobhoff or peg occurs at 10%
loss of body weight.

12
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:45,500
We want to avoid this for many reasons,
and the best way to do this is to commit

13
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,416
to eating real and complete foods
routinely from the start of treatment.

14
00:00:51,083 --> 00:00:54,250
Nonetheless, despite our best efforts,

15
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:57,791
there are times when a feeding tube
insertion is the best

16
00:00:57,791 --> 00:01:01,916
and only option for you to be able
to get adequate caloric intake.

17
00:01:02,291 --> 00:01:05,791
If this happens,
we will safely walk you through the steps

18
00:01:05,791 --> 00:01:09,375
of having the feeding
tube placed to best help you.

19
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:11,291
Thank you for watching.
